    "created_at": "2023-09-28T08:06:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-09-28T08:06:26Z",
    "body": "Because only tasks are defined as being able to cross the boundary and microtasks are queued and drained within the context of a single task.\r\n\r\nIf we didn't enforce this you could get random microtasks inserted coming in hot from another thread/process. That seems bad?\r\n\r\nI'm not entirely sure what we'd assert. We don't really have a concept of a current task.",
