    "body": "> Because only tasks are defined as being able to cross the boundary\r\n\r\nWhere is this defined?\r\n\r\n> If we didn't enforce this you could get random microtasks inserted coming in hot from another thread/process. That seems bad?\r\n\r\nWhy is this bad? From an architectural perspective microtasks are basically just another type of task... there's no reason to think they're any more thread-bound or \"hot\".\r\n\r\n> I'm not entirely sure what we'd assert.\r\n\r\nWe could assert that there is a surrounding agent.",
