    "created_at": "2023-09-28T08:59:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-09-28T08:59:16Z",
    "body": "Microtasks being scheduled without a task being around would be just wrong. Nothing guarantees there will be a task ever, so such microtask might not get executed ever. So, somehow we do need a task to be around. I think I'd prefer to assert that there is current task when scheduling a microtask.",
